# CSS Standards

## Architecture

- Single stylesheet: `style.css`. Use existing patterns before adding new abstractions.
- Design tokens live in `:root` (e.g. `--radius`, `--glitchedOpacity`). Extend tokens rather than scattering raw values.

## Naming (BEM + Underscores)

```
.block_name {}
.block_name__element {}
.block_name__element--modifier {}
```

Examples: `bar_top`, `settings_panel__line`, `list_answers__item--avatar`.

## Responsive

- Mobile breakpoint: `640px`.
- Utility classes: `hide_desktop`, `hide_mobile` — reuse them instead of duplicating media queries.

## JavaScript Hooks

- **Never style `.js-*` classes.** Style the structural BEM class; keep `js-` for behavior only.

## Transitions & Effects

- Reuse `default_transition` for interactive elements.
- Glitch mode: `body.glitched`, `body.glitched_halfgame`, `.text_symbol`, `.text_no_glitch` / `.text_glitch`.
- State visibility: prefer `.visible` / `.hidden` / `.visually_hidden` over `display: none` hacks unless the pattern already exists.

## Quality Bar

```css
/* ❌ BAD — overrides specificity war */
.foo { color: red !important; }

/* ✅ GOOD — use existing modifier or add a purposeful one */
.track_display__name--highlight { color: var(--accent); }
```

- Prefer flexbox patterns already used in `#wrapper`, `.panel_box`, `.track_display`.
- Keep `box-sizing: border-box` inherited; do not reset globally without reason.
